  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Barton is a 52-year-old nurse and relief-agency director with recurrent major depression, in remission on sertraline 100 mg for about four months, who comes for her periodic preventive visit. She completed the health risk assessment before the visit. Her back pain settled within two weeks of the July visit, and she took ibuprofen for five days. She has finished her course of cognitive behavioral therapy and attends a monthly peer support group for relief workers. She works about 45 hours a week, sleeps about seven hours, and walks most days. She has not been deployed and has agreed with her board that she will not return to field work before the spring. She has had no suicidal thoughts. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 52</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls, emergency visits, or hospital stays this year</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 100 mg daily without missed doses; ibuprofen for five days in July; no supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Recurrent major depression in remission; back strain resolved</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Full duties at about 45 hours a week; independent in all activities</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, much better than in January</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Sees friends weekly; monthly peer support group; weekly services with her faith community</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>One glass of wine a week (AUDIT-C 1); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Brisk walking about 150 minutes a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals again; weight back to her usual</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Smoke detectors working; no firearms in the home; medicines stored in a closed cabinet</td></tr><tr><td>Work</td><td>45-hour week; delegates the families&apos; correspondence; no deployment planned before the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

