<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic preventive visit, age 52</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Ten-year cardiovascular risk is about 1.5 percent by the pooled cohort equations, so a statin is not recommended. HbA1c 5.4 percent. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder, recurrent, in sustained remission (F33.1)</content>. PHQ-9 3, about four months in remission on sertraline 100 mg. Safety reviewed: no suicidal thoughts, intent, or plan; protective factors stronger than at intake. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 100 mg for at least twelve months after remission, then decide together about tapering or longer maintenance, given two or more episodes.</item><item>PHQ-9 every two to three months in continuation; collaborative safety plan reviewed and unchanged, with the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline and the clinic number.</item><item>Plan with her board for a return to field work in the spring: a shorter first deployment, a named peer contact, and a check-in visit before and after.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/72 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 196, HDL 64, LDL 112, triglycerides 98 mg/dL; ten-year risk about 1.5 percent, so no statin; repeat in five years</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>HbA1c 5.4 percent; repeat in three years if risk factors develop</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Last mammogram before her deployment, more than two years ago; biennial screening from 40 to 74; booked for next week</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HPV and cytology co-test negative three years ago, before deployment; next due in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No prior screening; options discussed and she chose colonoscopy, which is booked</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Postmenopausal and under 65; FRAX ten-year major osteoporotic fracture risk 5.2 percent, below the threshold for bone density testing</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening and monitoring</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 3 in continuation treatment; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Anxiety screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>GAD-7 2</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Both negative at her agency&apos;s occupational health screening after her return, before this year&apos;s care began</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Vaccinated as a nurse, with immunity documented by her occupational health service</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; a single dose is recommended for adults 50 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 given today; dose 2 in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; she will have it at her workplace clinic next week</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap before her deployment, two years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Due</td><td>No dental visit since her return; she will book one</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Mammogram next week and colonoscopy as booked. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Depression review with PHQ-9 in about two months. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
